Howdy fellow nethackers,

	I had this terrible thing happen to me.  I ran into this black dragon
on about the seventh level or so, only it wasn't a black dragon.  It was (you
guessed it) a chameleon.  So I'm about to teleport away, but I'm hungry, so I
figured I was dead.  Au contraire, at that second the Chameleon changed it's
form to that of a large dog. "Great!" I say to myself while throwing a tripe
ration at it.  So I have this tame Chameleon.  Cool, until 2 turns later it
changes into a newt and gets killed by a grid bug. Arrrrgh!!

	A few questions, though.  Does you luck increase when you throw a gem
at a tame unicorn (via polymorph trap).  Also, why do tame unicorns not eat
anything, but always wind up starving?  Also what is the correct way to get
into Wizard mode (on Nethack 3.0 pl8 on an Amiga).  Also, is the scroll you
read that creates all these monsters (specifically asking you what to create) a
blessed scroll of create monster or a cursed scroll of genocide?
 
	Also, don't you hate it when you step into a shop, kill off a ghost,
find a +8 athame, a +5 stormbringer and gauntlets of power only to be killed by
that same damn giant mimic that killed you before? Arrrgh!  Also, I really like
these water demons that gate in Demon Lords like Yeenoghu and Jubilex.  Like
they don't have something better to do on level 40. :)



Thanks,
Larry Gordon

